    // Tier 2 (medium, short-period) is the PRIMARY perceived motion --
    // it dominates by weight (u_midSwellStrength) and by having the
    // shortest period among the structural tiers, so its phase visibly
    // advances within any 1-2 second glance. Tier 1 (large, slow) is a
    // minor background contribution. Tier 3 (fast fine ripple) is kept
    // as its own separate term (fineField, not folded into waveField)
    // because its much shorter wavelength gives it a naturally much
    // larger gradient per unit height -- keeping it separate lets the
    // normal-composition line below weight it independently, so it reads
    // as "small ripples constantly moving" rather than overwhelming the
    // broad highlight with noise. waveHeight combines both for color/tone
    // and is scaled down since the raw sum of all three tiers can reach
    // roughly +/-2.3.
    // Directional advection of the SOURCE coordinate each tier samples
    // from -- distinct from (additive to) the phase-based motion already
    // inside waveComponent. Each tier's advection direction is chosen to
    // differ from that tier's own internal wave-component directions, so
    // this is a genuine additional relative-drift cue (the whole
    // interference pattern sliding, tiers sliding relative to each other)
    // rather than just accelerating an existing direction. This is what
